---
metadata:
  title: "Mr & Mrs Charles Dickens: Her Story | A Novel by Annie Elliot"
  description: "Discover the untold story of Mrs Dickens. Annie Elliot's historical novel reveals the life of Catherine Dickens, the woman behind the famous author."
  canonical: "https://annieelliot.co.uk/"
  pageType: "book"
---

<section id="about" class="u-container">
	<h1>Mr & Mrs Charles Dickens: <span>Her Story...</span></h1>
	<h2>So the world may know he loved me once</h2>
	<!--
		Inert, like the retailer buttons below: the line stays on the page, but
		nothing here links out while the listing is dormant. Canonical targets, for
		whoever turns these back into links — the originals carried long tracking
		query strings, which are in git history if they are wanted:
		Amazon      https://www.amazon.co.uk/dp/1915023742/
		Waterstones https://www.waterstones.com/book/mr-and-mrs-charles-dickens/annie-elliot/9781915023742
	-->
	<div class="amazon-tagline">
		<span class="amazon-tagline__inert">
			<span class="stars">★★★★★</span> 5 stars on amazon
		</span>
	</div>
	<div>
		<div class="u-grid main-grid">
			<div class="cover">
				<!--
					Inline rather than an <img src="…svg">: an SVG referenced by <img> is
					an isolated document that may not load the page's @font-face faces, so
					the title would silently fall back to a system font. Inlined, it draws
					in Playfair/Crimson/Barlow like the rest of the page, and costs no
					request and no sharp transcode.
				-->
				<svg
					class="cover__placeholder"
					viewBox="0 0 1000 1500"
					role="img"
					aria-labelledby="cover-placeholder-title"
				>
					<title id="cover-placeholder-title">
						Mr &amp; Mrs Charles Dickens: Her Story, a novel by Annie Elliot —
						cover coming soon
					</title>

					<rect width="1000" height="1500" class="cover__ground" />
					<rect
						x="34"
						y="34"
						width="932"
						height="1432"
						class="cover__rule cover__frame"
					/>
					<rect
						x="52"
						y="52"
						width="896"
						height="1396"
						class="cover__rule cover__frame cover__frame--inner"
					/>

					<text class="cover__title" x="500" y="440">MR &amp; MRS</text>
					<text class="cover__title" x="500" y="538">CHARLES DICKENS</text>
					<text class="cover__tagline" x="500" y="638">Her story&#8230;</text>

					<line x1="400" y1="730" x2="600" y2="730" class="cover__rule" />

					<text class="cover__byline" x="500" y="828">A NOVEL BY</text>
					<text class="cover__author" x="500" y="908">ANNIE ELLIOT</text>

					<!--
						Anchored near the bottom frame rather than floated under the
						byline: the slack then reads as deliberate space between two
						blocks, not as a hole in the middle of one.
					-->
					<line x1="300" y1="1240" x2="700" y2="1240" class="cover__rule" />
					<text class="cover__status" x="500" y="1332">COMING SOON</text>
					<line x1="300" y1="1380" x2="700" y2="1380" class="cover__rule" />
				</svg>
			</div>

			<div class="about-grid__prose">
				<p>
					After twenty-two years of marriage, the world-famous author banished
					Mrs Dickens (Catherine) from their home with their nine children and
					wrecked her reputation to protect his own when he fell in love with an
					eighteen-year-old actress.
				</p>

				<p>
					This is Kate's story: a poignant self-portrait of a woman struggling
					to achieve peace of mind by making sense of a marriage that defined,
					but nearly destroyed her. Sifting through her husband's letters after
					his sudden death she relives the happy times they shared but also
					speaks up for herself to expose the darker side of the man the world
					reveres.
				</p>

				<p>
					On her deathbed, Kate asked her daughter to give Charles's letters to
					the British Museum 'so the world may know he loved me once.' This
					novel fulfils her dying wish and restores her to history as more than
					a famous author's discarded wife. It bestows on Kate the respect,
					dignity, agency and voice she was denied in life.
				</p>

				<p class="button-note">Available to order soon</p>
				<div class="button-container">
					<button
						type="button"
						class="btn btn-waterstones"
						aria-label="Buy from Waterstones — coming soon"
						disabled
					>
						<img src="/images/waterstones-logo.svg" alt="Waterstones" />
					</button>
					<button
						type="button"
						class="btn btn-amazon"
						aria-label="Buy from Amazon — coming soon"
						disabled
					>
						<img src="/images/amazon-logo.svg" alt="Amazon" />
					</button>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#about {
		padding-block: var(--space-l);

		h1,
		h2 {
			text-align: center;
			color: var(--taupe);
		}

		h1 {
			margin: 0;
			font-family: var(--font-base);

			span {
				font-size: var(--step-3);
			}
		}

		h2 {
			margin-top: var(--space-s);
			margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
			font-size: var(--step-2);
			font-weight: normal;
			font-family: var(--font-condensed);
		}

		.amazon-tagline {
			text-align: center;
			font-family: var(--font-condensed);
			font-size: var(--step-0);
			margin-bottom: var(--space-l);
			letter-spacing: 0.05em;
			text-transform: uppercase;

			.amazon-tagline__inert {
				color: var(--taupe);
			}

			/*
				Greyed rather than Amazon orange: the line is inert, and the colour is
				what carries that now there is no link to lose. The `.btn:disabled`
				treatment (0.45 opacity) is not reused here — it would put this text at
				about 2.3:1 on cream, and unlike a disabled control, plain text gets no
				WCAG contrast exemption.
			*/
			.stars {
				color: var(--battleship-gray);
				margin-right: 0.5ch;
			}
		}

		p {
			text-align: justify;
		}

		.main-grid {
			gap: var(--space-2xl);
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			grid-template-areas:
				"cover"
				"prose";

			.cover {
				grid-area: cover;
			}

			.about-grid__prose {
				grid-area: prose;
			}

			@media all and (min-width: 60rem) {
				grid-template-columns: 3fr 2fr;
				grid-template-areas: "prose cover";

				.cover {
					position: sticky;
					align-self: start;
					top: var(--space-xl);
				}
			}

			.about-grid__prose > p:first-of-type {
				margin-top: 0;
			}

			.cover__placeholder {
				width: 100%;
				height: auto;
				display: block;
				box-shadow: 0 2px 12px var(--shadow-medium);

				.cover__ground {
					fill: var(--cream);
				}

				/* Strokes, not fills: `line` and the frame `rect`s are both outlines. */
				.cover__rule {
					fill: none;
					stroke: var(--light-beige);
					stroke-width: 3;
				}

				.cover__frame {
					stroke: var(--taupe);
				}

				.cover__frame--inner {
					stroke-width: 1;
					stroke: var(--light-beige);
				}

				text {
					fill: var(--taupe);
					text-anchor: middle;
				}

				.cover__title {
					font-family: var(--font-base);
					font-size: 78px;
					letter-spacing: 2px;
				}

				.cover__tagline {
					font-family: var(--font-italic);
					font-style: italic;
					font-size: 56px;
					fill: var(--battleship-gray);
				}

				.cover__byline,
				.cover__status {
					font-family: var(--font-condensed);
					text-transform: uppercase;
				}

				.cover__byline {
					font-size: 36px;
					letter-spacing: 10px;
					fill: var(--battleship-gray);
				}

				.cover__author {
					font-family: var(--font-base);
					font-size: 64px;
					letter-spacing: 4px;
				}

				.cover__status {
					font-size: 54px;
					font-weight: 700;
					letter-spacing: 14px;
				}
			}

			.launch-link {
				text-align: center;
				margin-top: var(--space-m);
				margin-bottom: var(--space-s);
				font-family: var(--font-condensed);
				font-size: var(--step-0);

				a {
					color: var(--taupe);
					font-weight: bold;
					text-decoration: underline;
					text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
					text-underline-offset: 2px;
				}

				a:hover {
					color: var(--black);
				}
			}

			.button-note {
				text-align: center;
				margin-top: var(--space-m);
				margin-bottom: 0;
				font-family: var(--font-condensed);
				font-size: var(--step-0);
				letter-spacing: 0.05em;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				color: var(--taupe);
			}

			.button-container {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
				gap: var(--space-xs);
				margin-top: var(--space-xs);
				max-width: 30rem;
				margin-inline: auto;
			}

			.btn {
				display: flex;
				justify-content: center;
				align-items: center;
				padding: var(--space-xs);
				border: none;
				border-radius: 4px;
				cursor: pointer;
				transition:
					transform 0.2s,
					opacity 0.2s;
				text-decoration: none;
				height: 50px;
				box-sizing: border-box;
				background-color: #ffffff; /* Ensure base background is white */
			}

			.btn:hover:not(:disabled) {
				transform: scale(1.05);
				opacity: 0.9;
			}

			/* Disabled until the new edition has a retailer to point at. */
			.btn:disabled {
				cursor: not-allowed;
				opacity: 0.45;
				filter: grayscale(1);
			}

			.btn img {
				max-height: 100%;
				max-width: 100%;
				object-fit: contain;
			}

			/* Specific adjustment for Amazon logo to make it larger */
			.btn-amazon img {
				transform: scale(1.2);
			}

			.btn-waterstones {
				background-color: #ffffff;
				border: 1px solid #000000;
			}

			.btn-amazon {
				background-color: #ffffff;
				border: 1px solid #ff9900;
			}
		}
	}
</style>
